		{
			"id": "109325739163426222",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://techhub.social/@tammymakesthings/109325739120795936",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tammy Makes Things",
				"url": "https://techhub.social/@tammymakesthings",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-11T14:53:12.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I think people didn’t realize when Facebook and Twitter were starting how much power we were giving the algorithms. And more importantly, how much incentive we were creating for people to try to manipulate the algorithms, and to shape what they said, for their own ends. Hopefully we don’t make the same mistakes here. 🤞</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109325740306269205",
			"parentId": 0,
