		{
			"id": "109325789770943083",
			"parentId": "109325768327161635",
			"url": "https://techhub.social/@tammymakesthings/109325788929348056",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tammy Makes Things",
				"url": "https://techhub.social/@tammymakesthings",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-11T15:05:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Human nature is that we shape our behavior to the incentives we’re given. And now a large swath of our society lives in a constant state of manufactured outrage. It’s one way to get that dopamine hit, for sure, but it’s so incredibly corrosive. I don’t think we realized that until much too late in the game.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
