			"date": "2022-11-11T15:08:49.223Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://techhub.social/@tammymakesthings\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>tammymakesthings</span></a></span> Yes! I just realized the parallel between this and leaving Facebook years ago—some of the same feelings happening.</p><p>(nature is healing)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109325851893704890",
			"parentId": "109325800519720132",
			"url": "https://techhub.social/@tammymakesthings/109325851429130199",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tammy Makes Things",
				"url": "https://techhub.social/@tammymakesthings",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-11T15:21:46.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I still have too many connections on Facebook that aren’t easily portable to leave it. (I’m realistically never going to get my mom to use Mastodon, for example.) But understanding the problem has definitely changed how I interact with the platform, which is a net good thing as long as I have to be there.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109325971518102746",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite/109325970794584098",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jared White (ResistanceNet ✊)",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/552/988/169/598/original/863bd81d9ad9d7b6.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2022-11-11T15:52:07.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> So true. It was getting to the point where I could post some thing helpful or interesting in some way, get almost zero engagement. Then post a hot take on something, boom 💥 goes semi-viral. Maybe at first that's a bit exciting, but then after a while, you realize you're just feeding the monster &amp; it's chipping away at your soul. Yikes! 😱</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
