			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@jaredwhite\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jaredwhite</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Twitter's algorithms encouraged controversy and argument. I will miss two things in the near term though:</p><p>1. The 15+ years worth of professional connections I built on there (and let's be honest DMs on here aren't great atm)</p><p>2. A place to promote my free developer events that actually reaches developers. The alternatives right now do not which is already making building awareness extra difficult.</p>",
