			"date": "2022-11-11T16:50:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://techhub.social/@tammymakesthings\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>tammymakesthings</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br>Shortly after I got on Twitter in ’09, I realized I could only really follow so many people, esp I followed accounts that tweeted a lot. Twitter came up with the algorithm that allowed me follow hundreds of accounts, with the algorithm picking which tweets I saw.  <br>We will have to develop our own tools here. I definitely don’t want an opaque algorithm designed to maximize my time on the site deciding. It seems like a problem with no easy answer.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
